/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Let a real signal have energy only between fL and fH, with bandwidth B = fH − fL.
   - 2fH/m ≤ fs ≤ 2fL/(m − 1)
   - Here m is an integer with 1 ≤ m ≤ ⌊fH/B⌋.
   - The largest m gives the lowest rate, fs = 2fH/m, which equals 2B when fH is an exact multiple of B.
   - A real sampler cannot take an impulse.
   - Flat-top sampling, done by a sample-and-hold circuit, holds each sample value constant for τ seconds.
   - Here τ is the hold time in s, f the frequency in Hz and sinc(u) = sin(πu)/(πu).
   - The magnitude |sinc(fτ)| is 1 at 0 Hz, falls across the band and reaches zero at f = 1/τ.
   - Two remedies are used.
*/
