/* book exam traps: Rejecting a valid band-pass rate because it is below 2fH. The low-pass condition is not the band-pass condition. | Taking fs = 2B and stopping there. It works only when fH is a multiple of B, and even then the copies touch; check 2fH/m ≤ fs ≤ 2fL/(m − 1). | Saying natural sampling causes the aperture effect. Natural sampling only scales each copy; flat-top (sample-and-hold) sampling distorts the band. | Confusing the hold time τ with the sampling period Ts. The first zero of sinc(fτ) is at 1/τ, which is fs only for a full-period hold. | Forgetting that 0.637 at fs/2 is for τ = Ts; at the top of a real signal band (below fs/2) the droop is smaller. */
