/* book exam traps: Using Δ as the maximum error. Inside the range the bound is Δ/2. | Writing L = 2ⁿ − 1. That is the largest code value; the number of levels is 2ⁿ. | Using 6.02n + 1.76 dB for a small or non-sinusoidal signal. It is for a full-scale sine with uniform error. | Mixing up the sign of the error: this book uses eq = Q(x) − x, so rounding 3.4 V up to 3.5 V gives +0.1 V. | Ignoring overload: outside xmin to xmax the output clips and Δ²/12 no longer describes the error. */
